          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Yang-Baxter equation
            (YBE) is, in some form or other, an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            reflection of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopy
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braids"} braids
          %p
            %br/
          #eq:TheIsotopy.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %code.maruku-mathml
          %div{:style => "margin: -50px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/3rdReidemeisterFramedLinks.png", :width => "400px"}/
          %p
            which is also known as the
            %em
              %a{:href => "braid+group#2ndArtinRelation"} 2nd Artin braid relation
            or the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3rd+Reidemeister+move"} 3rd Reidemeister move
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+links"} framed links
          %h3#quantum_ybe Quantum YBE
          %h4#plain_form Plain form
          %p
            Interpreting the isotopy
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheIsotopy"} (1)
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
